  "costAbout": "D.3 rows that need more than one rounding (purchase lines with Percent, foreign-currency entries, step pricing on lots, largest remainder, the D.1 composition) and the D.7 worked example. Consumed by xUnit (Domain/Costing RugCostMath + LargestRemainder; tests/RugsManagment.Tests/CostVectorsTests.cs) and by CostSql parity tests; a lib/num.ts consumer may adopt them op by op. Enum members are written by name.",
  "costOps": {
    "purchaseLines": "every purchase line of one rug: non-Percent lines first (Total: round(rate,s); PerM2: round(rate * pieceArea(intake),s) * qty; PerPiece: round(rate,s) * qty), then each Percent line = round(sum(non-Percent amounts) * rate / 100, s), once per line; 'amounts' in input order, 'total' = their sum",
    "entryPiece": "live cost entry per piece: PerM2 = round(rate * pieceArea, s), or with fx: round(round(rate * pieceArea, 2) * fx, s); PerPiece = round(rate, s), or with fx: round(rate * fx, s); line = piece * qty",
    "baseAmount": "Total entry or revenue: round(amount * (fx ?? 1), s) once, before any split",
    "stepPrice": "step pricing on a lot from the Priced* snapshot: Fixed/CustomFormula round(rate,s); PerSquareMeter round(rate * pieceArea, s); PerSquareFoot round(rate * pieceArea * 10.7639104, s); PerLength/PerWidth round(rate * L|W, s); Combined = sum of items each rounded per piece (no items given = Fixed; empty list = 0); line = piece * qty",
    "effectiveCost": "max(0, (manual ?? calculated ?? 0) + (adjustment ?? 0)); line-level, never times qty",
    "stepCost": "sum of effectiveCost over Completed and InProgress steps only",
    "lr": "largest remainder: A = |total| in units of 10^-scale; floor_i = A*w_i div W, rem_i = A*w_i mod W; the leftover units go to the largest rem_i, ties by larger weight, then lower serialSort (null last), then id as lowercase 'D' string, ordinal; sign of total reapplied; negative weights clamp to 0; all-zero weights split equally; 'shares' in member order",
    "compose": "D.1: purchaseCost = purchaseLines + purchaseAllocations; total = purchaseCost + stepCost + expenseAllocations; costPerM2 = round(total / totalAreaM2, s) or null when the area is 0; costPerPiece = round(total / qty, s)"
  },
